{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Hi support team, sorry to bother you with this, but it looks like our lab results feed hasn't updated since yesterday morning. Could someone take a quick look when you have a moment? Thanks so much.",
   "id": "gen-171",
   "subject": "Missing incoming lab feeds"
  },
  {
   "body": "Our lab feed stopped connecting this morning. Please reset the integration.",
   "id": "gen-172",
   "subject": "Lab interface connection down"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am looking over our monthly subscription statement and noticed a major discrepancy that I hope you can clear up. We were billed twice for the enterprise tier this month, and an extra user fee was added that we never authorized. I checked our internal roster and our provider count hasn't changed since last quarter. Please issue a refund for the duplicate charges and correct the invoice immediately so we can balance our accounts.",
   "id": "gen-173",
   "subject": "Incorrect charges and duplicate billing on monthly invoice"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am beyond frustrated because all of my custom medication favorites have completely disappeared from my profile again. I spent hours building out my preferred sigs and common drug lists, and after yesterday's software update, my entire list is blank. I tried clearing my cache and restarting the browser, but nothing brings them back. This slows down my charting immensely every single day, and I need someone to restore my saved preferences right away.",
   "id": "gen-174",
   "subject": "Medication favorites completely wiped out after update"
  },
  {
   "body": "We are trying to set up our new online medical history questionnaire for patients, but we keep running into a strange validation error on the birthdate field. I'm not sure which settings to adjust so patients can actually submit the form successfully without getting blocked. Could someone please clarify how the field validation rules are supposed to be configured?",
   "id": "gen-175",
   "subject": "Validation error on digital intake form fields"
  },
  {
   "body": "Reviewing our recent remittance advice, we have several insurance claim denials that need to be appealed with accompanying clinical notes. I pulled up the denial tracking report in the billing module, but I need instructions on how to attach the documentation directly to the electronic appeal submission. Please provide step-by-step guidance so our billers can re-file these promptly.",
   "id": "gen-176",
   "subject": "Attaching clinical notes to denied insurance claim appeals"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi there, apologies for the minor question, but I just want to make sure I am transmitting this new prescription correctly to the pharmacy network. Could you verify our connection is active? Thanks!",
   "id": "gen-177",
   "subject": "Quick check on electronic prescription transmission"
  },
  {
   "body": "Need to update a patient's preferred pharmacy since their usual location closed down. How do we search the directory and save a new entry?",
   "id": "gen-178",
   "subject": "Pharmacy directory search and update"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am at my wit's end trying to manage the sheer volume of portal messages coming in from patients every morning. The current routing rules seem completely broken because messages from pediatric patients are landing in our cardiology queue, and non-urgent appointment requests are going straight to the nursing staff. We have tried re-tagging the department filters three times this week, but the inbox is still a complete mess. Please look into our account settings and fix how these messages are distributed before a critical message gets missed.",
   "id": "gen-179",
   "subject": "Patient portal secure message routing is completely broken"
  },
  {
   "body": "Good morning, we are currently trying to run our batch of real-time insurance eligibility checks for tomorrow's scheduled appointments. However, several of our commercial payer verifications are timing out or returning connectivity errors when we query the clearinghouse. We have already verified our internet connection and restarted the workstation client. Could you please check if there are any known gateway issues with the eligibility service on your end today?",
   "id": "gen-180",
   "subject": "Real-time insurance eligibility verification timeouts"
  }
 ]
}
